# ---- Runtime artifacts (created by a running node / wallet) ----
# chain stores & JSON snapshots, wallet key files, the SPV light-wallet state,
# persisted soft state (peers / bans / mempool), a node config, and logs. The
# demos use temp dirs, but the README/QUICKSTART examples write these into the
# working dir.
chain*.json
chain*.db
*.db
wallet*.json
w*.json
spvwallet*.json
alice.json
bob.json
peers.json
bans.json
mempool.json
node.json
*.log
pid

# KEY MATERIAL. A node's identity key is a private key like the wallet's — it
# is created on first run beside -db (so it can land in a subdirectory, hence no
# leading slash) and committing it would publish the identity peers know a node
# by. Backups are key material too, encrypted or not.
nodekey*.json
dnas-backup*.json

# Light-client caches: the verified header chain (-cache) and the per-wallet
# copy each `spv wallet` keeps beside its state file. Derived from the chain and
# rebuilt on demand.
spvheaders*.json
*.headers

# The transaction files the multi-party flows pass between signers, and the
# receipts `dnas anchor add` leaves beside the file it anchored. Each is either
# a half-authorized transaction or a claim about someone's document — local
# working state, and in the sponsor/multisig case a spend somebody is still
# collecting signatures for.
multisig-spend*.json
escrow*.json
sponsored-tx*.json
invoice*.json
*.dnasanchor

# Every other .json in the REPOSITORY ROOT. The docs walk a reader through
# creating key files and half-signed transactions by name — m1.json, cold.json,
# buyer.json, spend.json, sig.json, bundle.json and a couple of dozen more — and
# enumerating them here goes stale the moment a new flow is documented. Nothing
# legitimately tracked lives at the root as .json today (the only committed one
# in the repo is .claude/launch.json, which this does not match). If that ever
# changes, add a `!name.json` exception below rather than dropping the rule.
/*.json

# ---- Go build output ----
# root-built binaries (go build -o dnas ./cmd/dnas), race build, and the TUI
# binaries; make writes to bin/ and dist/
/dnas
/dnas-tui
/dnas-race
tui/dnas-tui
tui/tui
/bin/
/dist/

# ---- Go test / coverage / profiling ----
# NOTE: testdata/fuzz/ is intentionally NOT ignored — Go's fuzz seed/regression
# corpus is committed; transient corpora live in GOCACHE, outside the repo.
*.test
coverage.out
*.coverprofile
*.prof
*.pprof

# ---- Python (gui/) ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# ---- Editor / IDE ----
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
# ---- OS cruft ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Misc temp ----
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig

# ---- Claude Code ----
# keep the shared .claude/launch.json committed; ignore per-user local settings
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json

